### Q2 — The Detector and Its Evidence (`L0`-`L3`, `N1`-`N20`)

* **Attack 6 — Discharge of ladder clause (i) and floor clauses (a), (b), (c) (`HOLDS`, READ / DERIVED):**
  * **Claim tested:** Do the five measured legs in Section 3 (`PACKET:165-173`) and `L0_TABLE:1-24` discharge ladder clause (i) and floor clauses (a), (b), and (c), including discharging (b) via `L0`?
  * **Defense check:**
    * **Clause (i) and floor (a):** Using the same frozen detector (`md5 6259ce546ddb88fbd1c27be5d091348d`, `PACKET:159`), `L0` runs pre-fix `base` (`md5 6c27af7b`) against the `FIX` column and exits `rc=1` with `LE_CSRMASK_CONTROL=OK` and `LE_CSRMASK_RESULT=17/20` (`PACKET:169`), failing exclusively the three CSR3 symptom rows: `N7` (`csr3 all`: got `0xffff`, head `0xffff`, fix `0x0007`, `L0_TABLE:9`), `N9` (`csr3 hi`: got `0x0008`, head `0x0008`, fix `0x0000`, `L0_TABLE:11`), and `N10` (`csr3 mix`: got `0x0015`, head `0x0015`, fix `0x0005`, `L0_TABLE:12`). `L1` runs `fix` (`md5 a82cd71f`) against the `FIX` column and exits `rc=0` with `LE_CSRMASK_CONTROL=OK` and `LE_CSRMASK_RESULT=20/20` (`PACKET:171`). `L2` runs both `base` vs `HEAD` (`20/20`) and `fix` vs `FIX` (`20/20`, `rc=0`, `PACKET:172`).
    * **Floor (b) via `L0`:** Because `H2` changes only comments (`DIFF:35-64`) and `H1` modifies only a single semantic site (`case 3: d->reg[r] = x & 0x0007;` vs. `default: d->reg[r] = x;`, `DIFF:12-33`), reinstating `d->reg[r] = x;` at that site yields a C translation unit semantically identical to `base` (`DERIVED`). Therefore, `L0` directly measures the single-site reversion required by clause (b).
    * **Floor (c):** `L3` runs `/bin/false` in GATE mode and produces `LE_CSRMASK_CONTROL=FAIL LE_CSRMASK_RESULT=0/20` with `rc=1` (`PACKET:170`), proving the harness fails `CONTROL` when the target medium does not run.

